Z||000009||ChadMan||05-31-2001||05:03 PM||||You know, it does look like there's a black hood scoop on that Fiero, too.  So we have two possibilities:<P>1)  This guy (gal?) has converted his Fiero to a front-engine setup.  The hood scoop ducts air to the carb/FI, and the fender scoop ducts cool air out of the engine bay.  He is a great backyard engineer and NOT guilty of ricing his Fiero (and is probably about to whoop this Mopar).<P>2)  This guy has tacked a big hood scoop on the front of his Fiero, which cools the spare tire.  The fender scoop does nothing, as there is no corresponding hole in the spaceframe underneath.  His Fiero is the San Francisco treat and is about to get stomped by this Mopar.<P>Any guesses as to which is true?||||reg||3
